{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "HDFC Bank Balance Sheet Analysis: Assets, Liabilities, Net Worth",
  "scenario": "You are an associate analyst at ICICI Securities reviewing HDFC Bank's balance sheet snapshots for FY22–FY24. Your manager asks you to compute total assets, total liabilities, net worth, and key ratios to assess the bank's funding mix and shareholder value creation. The numbers are in ₹ crore.",
  "instructions": "Build formulas in the Answers sheet to compute total assets, total liabilities, net worth, the debt-to-equity ratio, and identify the year with highest equity growth. Use SUM, SUMIF, and simple arithmetic on the Data sheet rows.",
  "learning_objective": "Compute a company's net worth from balance sheet components, calculate debt-to-equity ratios, and identify trends in shareholder value across fiscal years.",
  "hints": [
    "Total Assets = Current Assets + Non-current Assets. Current Assets are in rows 2–5; Non-current Assets are in rows 6–8.",
    "Total Liabilities = Current Liabilities + Non-current Liabilities. Current are rows 9–10; Non-current are rows 11–12. Then Net Worth = Total Assets − Total Liabilities.",
    "For Debt-to-Equity, use Total Liabilities ÷ Total Equity. For equity growth, compute (FY24 Equity − FY22 Equity) ÷ FY22 Equity as a percentage."
  ],
